Chapter: BvtKitSupplies
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-49 B: the testing kit's loose bandages, kindling and blank maps become the Britain catalog's items (clean
 bandages 75, kindling 119, blank map 117) when its tools are lotted, so Healing, Camping and Cartography accept them.
  bvt-kit-supplies : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-kit-supplies (unused) = act
    print-line-uni ("KITSUPPLIES bandages=" & show (cpr-kit-item cts-bandages) & " kindling=" & show (cpr-kit-item cts-kindling) & " map=" & show (cpr-kit-item cts-blank-map))
    a <- bvt-check "the kit's bandages, kindling and blank maps lot as clean bandages (75), kindling (119) and blank maps (117)" (cpr-kit-item cts-bandages == 75 & cpr-kit-item cts-kindling == 119 & cpr-kit-item cts-blank-map == 117 & cts-blank-map == cart-blank)
    b <- bvt-check "an art the kit does not carry as a material still lots as nothing (a blank scroll, 0x0E34)" (cpr-kit-item #0E34 == 0)
    a + b
  end
